  "label": "Political Rhetoric and Stereotypes",
  "description": "The phrase 'all American' is used ironically or sarcastically to imply that the person is a hypocrite or embodies negative traits associated with American values, such as greed, corruption, or moral decay. This is a common rhetorical device in political satire and criticism, often used to attack politicians perceived as out of touch or morally compromised.",
